That depends on whether you're one of the many classes that can do massive
ranged damage at melee range with stacked daggers or magic missile.
Personally, I think it's an excellent example; I'd much rather bounce an
XL30 MM off a wall and vaporise him. There's no penalty for overkill;
there is for underkill.

He can't teleport away if you can kill him in one shot. If you have the
Amulet and you throw it away he will teleport to it and pick it up. A
killer ranged attack is just the thing to have here; both because you want
the absolute maximum probability of oneshotting him and because you may be
able to arrange to engage him outside melee range.
